    "display_name": "Simulating a Viral Post",
    "long_instructions": "**Now, you’ll fix the program you saw in the previous level.**\r\n\r\nIt should simulate a post growing in views until it reaches a target number.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- Update `simulate` so that it simulates how many days it will take for a viral post’s `views` to reach `target`.\r\n- Ensure that, for each day, `simulate` prints a message in the format: `\"Day {day}: {views} views\"`.\r\n- Choose and experiment with different arguments to `simulate`. Pay attention to how they change your simulation’s outcome.\r\n\r\n**🖥️ Coding Tip:**\r\n\r\nRemember that Python’s `while` loop can repeat code while a condition is true. For example:\r\n\r\n```\r\ni = 1\r\nwhile i < 5:\r\n    print(i)\r\n    i += 1\r\n```",
